-- title:
--   Theorem 3.1, p. 1486 — μ(ã′x − b) ≤ 0 iff a′x ≥ b on conv{Aq : q ∈ 𝒬}; conversely every 𝒰 ⊆ conv(𝒜) arises from a coherent measure
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega = \{\omega_1, \dots, \omega_N\}$, $N \ge 1$, carry a probability vector $p$ with full support, and let the uncertain vector $\tilde a$ take the value $a_i \in \mathbb R^n$ at $\omega_i$ (Assumption 3.1); write $A = [a_1, \dots, a_N]$, so $Aq = \sum_i q_i a_i$, and fix $b \in \mathbb R$. For $x \in \mathbb R^n$, $\tilde a'x - b$ is the random variable $\omega_i \mapsto a_i'x - b$.
--
--   1. If $\mu$ is a coherent risk measure and $\mathcal Q$ is a generating family for $\mu$ (in the sense of (1), with $q \ll p$ for $q \in \mathcal Q$), then
--   $$\{x \in \mathbb R^n : \mu(\tilde a'x - b) \le 0\} = \{x \in \mathbb R^n : a'x \ge b \ \ \forall a \in \mathcal U\}, \qquad \mathcal U = \operatorname{conv}(\{Aq : q \in \mathcal Q\}). \tag{2}$$
--   2. Conversely, let $\mathcal U$ be a nonempty subset of $\operatorname{conv}(\mathcal A)$, $\mathcal A = \{a_1, \dots, a_N\}$, and let $\mathcal Q = \{q \in \Delta^N : \exists a \in \mathcal U,\ Aq = a\}$. Then $\mathcal Q$ generates a risk measure $\mu$, every risk measure generated by $\mathcal Q$ is coherent, and for it
--   $$\{x \in \mathbb R^n : \mu(\tilde a'x - b) \le 0\} = \{x \in \mathbb R^n : a'x \ge b \ \ \forall a \in \mathcal U\}.$$
--
--   The theorem turns a risk-aversion constraint $\mu(\tilde a'x - b) \le 0$ into an equivalent robust linear constraint with an explicit convex uncertainty set built from the generating family and the data, and shows that every uncertainty set inside the convex hull of the data arises this way.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The page prints $\mu(\tilde a'x - b) \ge 0$ in (2). The risk-aversion constraint is introduced on the same page as "$\mu(\tilde a'x - b) \le 0$", and the proof computes $\mu(\tilde a'x - b) = -\inf_{a \in \mathcal U} a'x + b$, so the set equality holds with $\le 0$ (with $\ge 0$ it fails already for $\mu(X) = \mathbb E[-X]$); the statement uses $\le 0$. "The family of generating measures for $\mu$" is read as any family satisfying (1). $\mathcal U \neq \emptyset$ is added in the converse: for $\mathcal U = \emptyset$ the family $\mathcal Q$ is empty and generates no real-valued $\mu$. Full support of $p$ is the reading discussed for Theorem 2.1. $n = 0$ is allowed.
-- source:
--   Bertsimas & Brown, Constructing uncertainty sets for robust linear optimization, Oper. Res. 57(6) (2009), p. 1486, Theorem 3.1, display (2); Assumption 3.1 and the risk aversion constraint μ(ã′x − b) ≤ 0, p. 1486

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RiskUncSets_Distortion_Setting

namespace RiskUncSets.Distortion

theorem theorem_3_1 {N : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (p : Fin N → ℝ) (hp : ∀ i, 0 < p i)
    (hp1 : ∑ i, p i = 1) {n : ℕ} (a : Fin N → Fin n → ℝ) (b : ℝ) :
    (∀ (μ : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℝ) (Q : Set (Fin N → ℝ)), IsCoherent μ → Generates Q μ →
        (∀ q ∈ Q, ∀ i, p i = 0 → q i = 0) →
        {x : Fin n → ℝ | μ (fun i => a i ⬝ᵥ x - b) ≤ 0} =
          {x | ∀ a' ∈ convexHull ℝ ((fun q : Fin N → ℝ => ∑ i, q i • a i) '' Q),
            b ≤ a' ⬝ᵥ x}) ∧
      (∀ U : Set (Fin n → ℝ), U.Nonempty → U ⊆ convexHull ℝ (Set.range a) →
        (∃ μ : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℝ,
          Generates {q | q ∈ stdSimplex ℝ (Fin N) ∧ ∃ a' ∈ U, ∑ i, q i • a i = a'} μ) ∧
        ∀ μ : (Fin N → ℝ) → ℝ,
          Generates {q | q ∈ stdSimplex ℝ (Fin N) ∧ ∃ a' ∈ U, ∑ i, q i • a i = a'} μ →
            IsCoherent μ ∧
              {x : Fin n → ℝ | μ (fun i => a i ⬝ᵥ x - b) ≤ 0} = {x | ∀ a' ∈ U, b ≤ a' ⬝ᵥ x}) := by sorry

end RiskUncSets.Distortion
